  "body": "## BLOCKED / needs_followup \u2014 do not merge\n\nThis remains an honest existing-corpus remediation gap PR, **not** a readiness or approval claim. It must remain OPEN + DRAFT until a wholly fresh Mennonite audits the exact live head and the unresolved authority gaps are closed.\n\n- **Target edition:** English 2014 first/release printing of *Dead of Winter: A Crossroads Game*, BGG 150376\n- **Excluded:** PH1000 except segregated comparison; The Long Night; Warring Colonies; promos/Raxxon; translations; digital adaptations\n- **Base:** `e0e47b2f7593f5ee34c25c5695be9b6bed172afd`\n- **Old audited SHA (Mennonite REVISE):** `0119e8d471005cc5155c32d6c3f7664db97c2532`\n- **Repaired exact head:** `29249965ba26645d57810584bf9d946db676be5a`\n- **Bathcat-Authored:** true\n- **Audit-Owner:** wholly fresh Mennonite context\n- **Disposition:** OPEN + DRAFT + `needs_followup`; Bathcat has not approved, promoted, marked ready, or merged\n\n## Edition/source ledger\n\n| Source | Receipt and scope |\n|---|---|\n| 2014 live Plaid Hat rulebook | HTTP 200, `application/pdf`, 24,044,267 bytes, 20 pages, SHA-256 `41f37d18f07bf04303c364916dcc0bab62d379b85373661650b0118be5812ca7`; InDesign CS6/PDF Library 10.0.1; created `2014-01-29T04:54:29Z`, modified `2014-01-29T04:55:24Z`; PDF 1.7, 576\u00d7756 pt. **Target primary authority.** |\n| 2014-04-24 Wayback PDF | HTTP 200, byte/hash-identical to the live target PDF. Immutable release-era witness. |\n| 2014-09-30 archived product page | HTTP 200 capture, 33,532 served bytes, SHA-256 `5ce72862a372daaea1d4684d6b2cbe71247b5926155bffa790f5fd35db72893f`; links the captured rules path as \u201cdownload the game rules.\u201d First-print mapping blocker closed. |\n| Official FAQ v1.1 | HTTP 200, 2,684,037 bytes, 4 pages, SHA-256 `331e65dc07240857405d595592e8320e61ac6649def735b3cb8c7659ba13bcee`; retained as target-applicable authority with its 2015-02-05 official announcement. Announcement HTML remains date/dynamic-receipt bounded. |\n| PH1000 | HTTP 200, 9,006,551 bytes, 20 pages, SHA-256 `0d7389eb286e454ff3fc431efc68fd87f5aceaba939e02bab55664e6183af9b9`; **later 2020 revised-print comparison only, never target authority.** |\n\nPH1000 changes now explicitly segregated: 30\u219220 zombie tokens; removal of the 2014 turn-only card-play sentence plus added event-item removal text; crisis threshold `number of players`\u2192`number of non-exiled players`; added general `Roll a Die` rule.\n\n## Corrected arithmetic and governing boundary\n\n- Printed component categories: **32/32** under one printed bullet = one category.\n- Target 2014 quantity total: **637**: `10+24+10+10+30+5+1+25+20+20+20+20+20+20+20+80+25+20+20+20+20+6+2+30+30+30+60+1+6+1+30+1=637`.\n- Target includes **30 zombie tokens**, not 20; no bag is listed.\n- Card/board/reference allocation: **341/341 physical card/board/reference components represented by class and quantity**, explicitly including colony board: `10+24+10+10+30+5+25+(6\u00d720)+20+80+6+1=341`.\n- Item cards: **145** (`25 + 6\u00d720`), not 170.\n- Distinct identity/text coverage, governing completeness, and any composite remain **UNKNOWN**; no governing percentage is claimed.\n- All 12 target OKFs remain `needs_followup`.\n\nOpen classes remain explicit: 10 dual-sided main objectives; 24 ordinary/10 betrayal/10 exiled objectives; 30 survivor abilities; 145 items; 20 crises; 80 Crossroads; 5 references; colony board + 6 locations; any other rule-bearing surfaces; and tokens/markers/dice/standees/first-player semantics only to the extent governed by the 2014 rulebook/FAQ.\n\n## Rule/reception repairs\n\nEvery substantive framework claim was rebound to the 2014 PDF and FAQ v1.1. Target crisis law now says **number of players**; PH1000's non-exiled-player threshold is disclosed only as a later-print difference, and FAQ v1.1 supplies no correction. Target turn-only card play and PH1000's later text change are explicit; the PH1000-only general `Roll a Die` rule is excluded from target law. The unsupported statement that frontmatter retained a 2\u20135 field was removed. The exile-vote tie statement now follows the 2014 first-player tie-break rule.\n\nReception remains one-review bounded: `randomness` is retained; `strategic-depth` is explicitly mapped from finite narrative supply to repeated-play discovery/planning uncertainty, not presented as consensus.\n\n## Visual packet\n\nAll four in-place references were rebuilt from target PDF pp. 2, 4, 6, and 12 with documented deterministic reduced editorial-excerpt transforms (Poppler 25.03.0, 72 dpi PNG; FFmpeg 7.1.5/libwebp, Lanczos 458\u00d7600, q55, compression 6, metadata removed). The 2\u00d72 contact sheet is built only from the retained derivatives.\n\n| Artifact | Dimensions | Bytes | SHA-256 |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| `01-setup.webp` | 458\u00d7600 | 40,546 | `84f1c46c097621d0d5c27250e97e237aae394967ea0dd07236100b234dd3b1b5` |\n| `02-loop.webp` | 458\u00d7600 | 42,694 | `69b4dd9560316f7b8f1407c2a7460d632b26aaf0979cc3818fdb94bb9ef27bc7` |\n| `03-tension.webp` | 458\u00d7600 | 41,324 | `6e3e6958678613ef3ac5c08d6356ece8f2499d6f5382e47222f3a0d8f94a0c74` |\n| `04-endgame.webp` | 458\u00d7600 | 49,464 | `b35ee3dc64664b6be1556a7b393e1b10088f7dad7d8e322d3f19066874aaff08` |\n| contact sheet | 458\u00d7600 | 44,654 | `ae160ead7e260fa935d20a70ff7911834dba9edd99fbe9bc6ae56ef27c578d92` |\n\nSame-turn inspection confirmed four distinct uncorrupted panels, target p. 2 visibly showing **30 zombie tokens**, and no PH1000/expansion/promo leakage. No additional photography is requested.\n\n## Files and validation\n\nRepair commit: 17 files changed \u2014 10 target OKFs, four in-place visual references, contact sheet, visual manifest, and telemetry. Full PR remains scoped to Dead of Winter records/visuals plus generated BoardGames index and telemetry.\n\n- focused 12-target OKF validation \u2014 clean\n- focused visual validator tests \u2014 5 pass, 0 fail\n- final ordered writer/gate pass: index generated; full OKF validation **2,619 clean + INDEX fresh**; prescribed Node suite **31 pass, 0 fail, 1 skip**; diff-aware intake gate clean; `git diff --check` clean\n- normal pre-push hook repeated intake/provenance suite and diff-aware gate \u2014 clean\n- exact-head CI: [run 30621063605](https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30621063605) / [job 91125474191](https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30621063605/job/91125474191), `head_sha=64e4dfaf2332e0957ed95a1b33b2c49442d27e3e`, substantive steps executed, **SUCCESS**\n\n## Residual HOLD / exact help requested from T\n\n1. Provide or authorize an authoritative bounded live/archived Fantasy Flight Games support inventory beyond the inspected captures.\n2. Provide a lawful immutable complete 2014 base-game card/board/reference face corpus, or a physical copy for independent inspection without publishing replacement-quality text.\n\n**Remain DRAFT, OPEN, `needs_followup`, and unmerged. Receiver: Judge, then a wholly fresh Mennonite audit bound to `29249965ba26645d57810584bf9d946db676be5a`.**\n",
